Package: draftright
Version: 2.4.1
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10),
         python3-gi,
         python3-requests,
         gir1.2-gtk-4.0,
         gir1.2-adw-1,
         gir1.2-gtk-3.0,
         gir1.2-ayatanaappindicator3-0.1,
         xdotool,
         xsel
Recommends: xclip,
            python3-xlib,
            wl-clipboard,
            xdg-desktop-portal
Maintainer: Tan Nguyen <tan@draftright.app>
Homepage: https://draftright.app
Description: AI-powered text rewriting tool
 DraftRight lets you select text anywhere on your desktop, pick a tone,
 and get a polished rewrite instantly. Supports professional, casual,
 friendly, concise, formal, and translation modes.
 .
 Press a global hotkey to capture your selection, choose a tone from
 the floating panel, and replace or copy the result.
 .
 Dependency notes: gir1.2-gtk-3.0 and gir1.2-ayatanaappindicator3-0.1 are
 required by the tray helper, which runs as a separate GTK3 process because
 AppIndicator cannot be loaded into the GTK4 app. python3-xlib is needed for
 the X11 global hotkey, wl-clipboard for the Wayland clipboard, and
 xdg-desktop-portal for the Wayland global shortcut; each degrades gracefully
 when absent, which is why they are Recommends rather than Depends.
